From what I read in another thread on Medusa, the difference is simply
in whether your character is visible or invisible. In the first case,
her reflected gaze will kill her, in the second, she will not notice her
gaze being reflected. There is some logic in this. In the 0.0.7E6F3
wizard-mode game, I was indeed visible, in the 0.7E7F3 one invisible (I
took old wizard-mode games, in which I had tried out other things to
check on this point; obviously, one should prepare the two debugging
games precisely the same way when trying to make a comparison... :-) :-( )

In fact, I must have been invisible several times when meeting Medusa in
real game. But since I was blindfolded, I did not get the message of her
not noticing her reflected gaze, and I did not always pay attention to
whether I had reflection or not.


